# Orthogonal Wilson spatial records in the fixed source charge frame

This is a new declared spatial family extending the frozen finite
`native_orthogonal_wilson_bridge`, not a reinterpretation of the original
beta-Wilson source. It uses the same native spectral mass m, four complete
native constituents per vertex, original canonical field Psi, full rho,
old/dual/port/spin references, normalized Gauss map Y and global code guard.
Take a=1/m, g=1/64 and the bridge's positive completion coefficient c=21/2.
Only the finite box and total photon cap vary. The field, charge labels,
reference cost4|R|, literal finite Peierls exponentials and outer-constraint
extension are exactly those of the admitted spatial family.

The changed terms are explicit in this fixed field:

`h_perp,xx/m=beta+degree(x) Gamma/2`,
`h_perp,tail head/m=-(Gamma+i alpha_j)/2`,
`Gamma=alpha_1 alpha_2 alpha_3 beta`.

The original beta-sea scalar is retained. No perpendicular vacuum energy is
silently subtracted. Each finite source retains every native complement and
all zero-energy reference spectators. The theorem below concerns complete
records of a prepared perpendicular free sea, not its coupled ground.

## A uniform free one-body gap and a physical preparation map

Let W be the actual vertex graph Laplacian divided by2, and K the Hermitian
alpha-derivative part, both dimensionless. W>=0, ||W||<=6, and {beta,K}=0.
For 0<=theta<=pi/2 use the exact finite-graph homotopy

`h_theta/m=beta+A_theta`,
`A_theta=K+(cos(theta) beta+sin(theta) Gamma)W`.

All spin matrices commute with W, but K and W need not commute at an open
boundary. The correct operator identity is

`(h_theta/m)^2=I+2 cos(theta)W+A_theta^2 >= I`.       (1)

Thus no boundary commutation premise is used. The gap is at least m on every
finite graph and all along the homotopy. The positive and negative ranks stay
2V each. Also ||h_theta/m||<=10 and ||d_theta(h_theta/m)||<=6.

Let P_theta be its negative projector. The off-diagonal differentiated
spectral equation is a Sylvester equation between spectra separated by2m.
Its convergent semigroup integral gives ||P'_theta||<=3. The anti-Hermitian
Kato generator `[P'_theta,P_theta]` has the same norm and its unitary U_theta
satisfies `U_theta P_0 U_theta†=P_theta`. This mathematical transport is
used for rank/gap reasoning, not as the executed apparatus service. It
does not rely on the cube's numerical projector-angle bound or
on an unproved uniform principal direct rotation.

For a finite algebraic controller prescription, choose lexicographic
Gram-Schmidt bases for the negative and positive ranges of each endpoint
projector, and set `U_alg=V_perp,- V_beta,-†+V_perp,+ V_beta,+†`.
The gap/rank proof ensures equal dimensions, and this unitary maps P_beta
to P_perp exactly. The endpoint matrices and projectors are algebraic, so
the basis rule is a finite spectral/arithmetic service. This is the chosen
preparation service below; it produces the same filled-sea state as Kato
transport up to one overall phase. No continuous homotopy clock or extra
physical field is used to execute the pulse.

The number-preserving Fock lift R of U_alg is defined with the unambiguous
annihilator convention

`R† Psi R=U_alg Psi`,

so the state R|Omega_beta> has covariance P_perp. It commutes with total
charge, though generally not with local density. Psi, rho and Y remain the
same operators. Its physical implementation is `Y R Y†`, identity on the
outer-constraint complement; R is identity on the native code complement.

Use the parent's independent full-box banks, all local code-admission bits
and first-success routing. After routing, compose this physical sea rotation
into that same declared finite routing pulse. On every successful fine flag
pattern the active source factor is exactly Omega_perp times the photon
vacuum, with its actual Gauss labels. All failed banks and original spin
references remain. The original success bound `1-V(1-p0^4)^R` is unchanged.
The three preparation slots cancel the actual new source Hamiltonian; this
is not evolution under the old clock or an implicit free pause.

## The exact symmetry needed by the state proof

The source charge-conjugation matrix `C0=i beta alpha_2` obeys

`C0 beta* C0†=-beta`, `C0 Gamma* C0†=-Gamma`,
`C0 alpha_j* C0†=alpha_j`.

For every finite open box, the literal matrices consequently satisfy

`C0 h_perp* C0†=-h_perp`,
`C0 J_e* C0†=J_e`, `Tr J_e=0`.

Here C0 is applied onsite. Functional calculus gives
`C0 P_perp* C0†=I-P_perp`. Since a Hermitian current expectation is real,
`Tr(P_perp J_e)=0`; similarly `Tr(P_perp P_x)=2`. Thus every bare hopping
expectation is real, every onsite mean density is zero, and the same exact
Slater variance bound `||sum a_x rho_x Omega_perp||<=2||a||_2` holds.
These identities replace the ordinary time-reversal argument used in the
original source. No new classical scalar background or native state is used.

Ordinary parity with spin matrix beta and ordinary spin time reversal each
reverse the Gamma regulator and fail at finite spacing. Their combined
finite-box antiunitary, with spatial inversion and spin matrix beta T0,
preserves the free one-body operator and has square -I. These statements
are checked on the actual degree-dependent open-box matrix. They are not
claims that a fixed charged boundary reference preserves spatial inversion,
or that the whole native complement inherits a continuous physical spin or
time-reversal representation. The one-body C identity is sufficient for the
prepared-state limits and zero-current assertion here.

## Positive-time local record convergence with fresh state data

The photon/cochain family is unchanged, including the total-cap boundary
completion and its finite CCR defect. The current bonds remain rank-two
partial isometries of norm1. All Gauss, phase/current and continuity
identities remain literal, with the new B. Every onsite spin rotation still
preserves local charge. Thus the uniform commutator majorant has the same
row bound `16+8g+4g^2`, and the same bounded-hopping spatial truncation applies
on the invariant code. It is not a full-native locality theorem.

The prepared matter state is freshly P_perp. Equation(1) and ||h||<=10 give
the same sign-polynomial error `100(99/100)^(J+1)`, with finite-range powers
agreeing away from the open boundary. Therefore its local projector has a
controlled bulk limit. The vanishing mean density and the same Slater
variance prove the same l2 longitudinal-dipole tail, including insertions:
for a k-factor CAR word the error is at most `(2+k)||delta a||_2`.

The transverse Q covariance, full electric/magnetic covariances and exact
Weyl phases use the unchanged three-dimensional Hodge operator. Their
uniform heat tails, including Q's `12/T`, are unchanged. Freely evolved
hopping has the same Coulomb phase

`g^2 t[(D G rho_ref)_e+(D G D^T)_ee/2]`,

with the actual new onsite matrices. The baseline retains the complete
quadratic field and Coulomb energy. Only bounded hopping terms are removed
in the spatial comparison. Each retained free Dyson word converges by the
fresh P_perp projector, the dipole estimate and the common photon covariance;
the same absolute Dyson tail then controls complete local histories.

Consequently the actual finite members, prepared as above with the parent's
vanishing admission-failure and literal finite-cap schedules, have complete
positive-time local E/B and bounded current record limits at fixed spacing.
All success/failure and detector outcomes are retained. The observer recedes
from all six box faces; the arbitrary reference root term vanishes only on
the total-charge-zero history sector. No differently sized sharp Gauss
fibers are asserted to be literal nested physical Hilbert subspaces.

## A fresh strict current interaction witness

For the new bulk symbol, set `A=3-cos q_j-cos q_k` and

`E_perp^2=1+sum sin^2 q_i+(3-sum cos q_i)^2`.

The actual bare hopping contraction is again
`f_perp=integral(A cos q_e-1)/E_perp`. Direct integration by parts gives

`f_perp=-integral[(A cos q_e-1)^2+1+sin^2 q_j+sin^2 q_k]/E_perp^3`.

Now `E_perp^2<=37<49`; the numerator's last three terms have mean2.
Therefore `-f_perp>=2/343`. This is a fresh source contraction, not reuse of
the old or cube current-square number. The unchanged photon variance bound
v_Q<13 and the finite sign-projector error give, at J=2048,

`[2/343-400(99/100)^2049]*(1-13/8192)>1/173`.           (2)

The selected edge must be farther than4097 from all faces, as before.

The full physical electric kick shifts just that link by exp(-ig), because
P_T+DGD^T=I. The new onsite matrix has norm at most4, the same eleven-edge
current bound holds, and the C identity gives initial current mean zero.
The complete moment/domain proof of the parent witness therefore yields
`|d<sin(uJ)>/d tau|<=512u` on either kicked or un-kicked state, including
the exp(ivJ)-conjugated states in the sine derivative.

With kick strength1, u=2^-16 and the actual wait tau=2^-32, the matched
setting-conditioned probability contrast is at least

`L_perp=(u/2)[g/173-(64/3)u^2-1024tau]>0`.             (3)

Its g=0 comparison is exactly zero. The actual current still has full Fock
spectrum within {-2,-1,0,1,2}, so its bounded readout is a degree-four
polynomial with coefficient/norm weight at most515. The same fresh finite
budget uses `s=2+4g sqrt(N/(4sqrt2))` and ten additional accuracy bits.
For the explicit n=8200 box, seven banks and K=363595359 suffice. All native
and photon matrices at that size are analytic, not numerically enumerated.

If f_n and d_n denote the actual admission failure and complete cap error,
the complete fair-setting/success/outcome law obeys

`TV(law_g,law_0)>=(1-f_n)L_perp/2-2d_n`.

The limiting separation is at least L_perp/2. This witnesses a coupled
nonstationary local current response in the revised spatial family. It does
not identify a charged pole, interacting vacuum mass or scattering matrix.

## What the cube ground and the free common cone do not transfer

The retained beta-sea scalar has a real, volume-dependent effect. On the
free code, the new vacuum raw shift is
`Delta_n=m(S_beta,n-S_perp,n)`. Its bulk density satisfies

`lim Delta_n/(m V)=2 integral(E_beta-E_perp)>=6/7`.

Indeed `E_beta^2-E_perp^2=2W`, both energies are at most7, and the mean W
is3. The finite-range sign polynomial proves this normalized-trace limit;
one explicit error is `8000(99/100)^(J+1)+80 b_n`, where b_n is the
fraction of vertices within2J+2 of a face. At fixed c=21/2 the one-bad-cell
native complement costs only mc above its native baseline. One noncode
constituent makes P_all zero, switching off the whole guarded kinetic and
Peierls correction; it does not pay cV. The unguarded positive field,
Coulomb and reference operators remain. Thus, already at
g=0, sufficiently large boxes have a lower complement state than the
perpendicular code vacuum. The small cube's full-ground theorem is not
uniform in volume. At nonzero coupling no larger-box ground assignment is
inferred. A separately declared counterterm/completion would be needed for
a ground-based spatial construction; it would change raw energy comparisons.
The explicit countercontrol uses J=2048 and N=2^24 vertices per axis;
`b_n<=6(2J+2)/N` gives a shift density greater than1/2. The frozen native
one-triplet excitation costs less than m, so `Delta_n>m(c+1)` strictly
undercuts the code by the actual one-bad-cell complement state. No huge
matrix is executed for this analytic example.

There is a concrete source-only ground-sector repair option. This is a
separately declared completion, not part of the fixed-c family above.
Choose as a variational state exactly the two beta-negative canonical
occupations at every vertex, with photon vacuum. The complete occupation
code contains this Slater state in the fixed Psi representation. It has
rho_x=0 as an exact eigenvalue at every site, so Y attaches zero longitudinal
and total-reference labels and every Coulomb/reference cost is zero.
Every intersite fermion contraction vanishes, hence every Peierls hopping
expectation is zero at every finite cap and any g. Since Gamma anticommutes
with beta, its onsite expectation is zero, while the mass term contributes
-2mV. Retaining the old scalar gives the exact trial energy

`E_trial=E_base+m(S_beta,n-2V)<=E_base+18mV`.

The final inequality uses the source's2V positive beta levels and
||h_beta/m||<=10. Therefore the declared choice

`c(N)=18V+1`

puts every physical native-code-complement state at least m above this
variational upper bound. It selects the code as the physical ground sector
for each finite box and cap, without measured calibration or architecture
uniqueness. It neither identifies that coupled ground vector nor proves an
internal code gap or a ground-state volume limit. An exact source-computed
upper bound on S_beta,n-2V gives the smaller sufficient ceiling rule
`c(N)=ceil(upper(S_beta,n-2V))+1`.

Every code pattern reduces the source and record instruments. Thus this
changed completion leaves the admitted code records above unchanged when
the finite controls cancel the stated new Hamiltonian; raw complement
energies and inter-pattern coherent phases do change. The raw control
bound replaces `(21/2)Vm` by `Vm c(N)` for this separate option. This
volume-dependent coefficient is a declared finite source family, not a
uniform full-native locality theorem. No assertion about the zero-valued
outer-Gauss-failure extension replaces the physical-sector comparison.

There is also a direct warning against transferring the free common cone to
interacting particle energies. In the unbounded-oscillator bulk comparison,
rotational
symmetry makes the link variance v the same on all axes. The exact photon
vacuum compression of the **kinetic matrix only** is

`h_vac(q)/m=beta+r alpha.sin(q)+Gamma[3-r sum cos q_i]`,
`r=exp(-g^2 v/2)`.

The transverse projector has local diagonal2/3 and its frequency is at most
sqrt12, so `v>=1/(3sqrt12)>0`; the proved upper bound is13. Therefore
`1/2<r<1`. This compression has a new Gamma rest term `3(1-r)` and its
small-momentum squared curvature is `3r-2r^2>1`. Gamma is allowed by the
remaining proper rotations, C and combined PT. The exact coefficient is
executed algebraically. This is not a full self-energy, charged excitation
or pole calculation: Coulomb correlations and virtual photon sectors remain
in the true source. Their cancellation or additional shifts must be proved,
not inferred from this compression or from the free cone.

## Full clock and resource custody

The complete witness clock remains `5+tau/m`, with the physical sea rotation
composed into the routing service and every failure retained. The exact
finite logarithm services cancel this new raw Hamiltonian during their five
slots. The original Psi/rho/Y frame is never silently reset.

A sufficient raw norm is the parent's B_raw plus `(89/2)Vm`: the new
second-quantized regulator differs by at most34Vm, and replacing the small
positive completion by21/2 costs at most(21/2)Vm. For R independent banks,
the five controls have norm at most `R B_raw,new+pi` and gross switching
work at most `10(R B_raw,new+pi)`. The source/reference/field/flag capacity
is unchanged; the new spectral-transport coefficients are additional finite
controller workspace, not included in that Hilbert capacity. No efficient
local compilation or memory-budget-selected volume is asserted.
The34Vm estimate can be obtained by an onsite/edge triangle sum, using
`||Gamma-beta||=sqrt2` and the full Fock norm of each individual phased
edge. It does not assume simultaneous diagonalization or commutation of
different finite-cap link coordinates.
